&+CDURIS RULES&n
&+c======================================================================&n
Read these rules before playing and check them for updates. Follow both
their wording and their intent. If anything is unclear, ask Staff through
&+Ypetition&n before acting. Not knowing a rule does not excuse breaking it.

&+C1. Fair play&n

   Players are expected to play fairly and in the spirit of the game. Do
   not exploit loopholes, game mechanics, or alternative characters to
   gain an unfair advantage over other players.

   Examples of prohibited behaviour include, but are not limited to:

   - Farming epics by camping epic stones, abusing broken quests, or
     purchasing epic bottles that grant more epics than they cost.

   - Keeping characters rented, camped, or voided solely for use as portal
     targets.

   - Using !risk or !frag alternative characters to gain a PvP advantage.

   - Using alternative characters to gather intelligence or reduce the
     risks that would otherwise be faced by a primary character.

   &+YImmortal discretion:&n These examples are not exhaustive. Immortals may
   exercise reasonable discretion when determining whether conduct
   violates the spirit of fair play, even where a specific action is not
   explicitly listed. Decisions should consider the circumstances, intent,
   and advantage gained, and should be applied fairly and consistently.

   The fact that something is technically possible within the game does
   not automatically make it permissible.

&+C2. Bugs and exploits&n
   Report bugs promptly with the &+Ybug&n command. If you are unsure whether
   something is a bug, ask Staff. Do not exploit bugs or help others exploit
   them; reporting a bug does not give permission to keep using it.
   Never deliberately crash, freeze, or disrupt the game. Report any bug
   that does so to Staff immediately, or as soon as you can reconnect.
   Keep exploit details off public channels and boards; report them to
   Staff privately through &+Ybug&n or &+Ypetition&n.

&+C3. Respect, privacy, and communication&n
   Treat players and Staff with respect. Harassment, hate speech, sexual
   harassment, real-world threats, blackmail, and extortion are prohibited.
   Do not share another person's private information without permission.
   Do not impersonate Staff or another player, or forge Staff messages.
   Do not spam or flood channels, tells, or commands. Keep disagreements
   civil; repeated abuse or disruptive complaints may result in a silence.

&+C4. Characters and multi-playing&n

   Players may only have one character logged into the game at any time,
   regardless of account, connection or device. Multi-playing is strictly
   prohibited.

   Players must not use characters on the opposite side of the racewar to
   gather information that provides an advantage to their own side,
   whether directly or indirectly. Players must not circumvent, or attempt
   to circumvent, the racewar login timer through alternative characters,
   accounts, connections or any other means.

   Account and character sharing policies will be determined in
   consultation with the playerbase. Until a formal policy is established,
   account sharing alone will not be treated as a rules violation. All
   other applicable rules remain enforceable regardless of who is
   controlling a character.

   Do not access another person's account or character without permission,
   steal passwords, or attempt to compromise accounts.

   See &+Yhelp multi-playing&n for further guidance.

&+C5. Robots and unattended play&n

   Scripts, triggers and automation are permitted, including unattended
   botting for skill development and repetitive skill training.

   Duris recognises that players have real-life commitments. Stepping away
   for bathroom breaks, family responsibilities, work meetings or other
   interruptions is perfectly acceptable. Players may use scripts or bot
   triggers to temporarily maintain their characters while otherwise
   occupied.

   Automation should supplement actual gameplay, not replace it entirely.
   While unattended skill development is expressly permitted, running a
   character continuously as a fully automated bot, with little or no
   genuine player involvement, is prohibited.

   Immortals may exercise reasonable discretion when assessing excessive
   automation, considering the overall pattern of play rather than
   isolated periods of inactivity.

   The intention is to accommodate real players, including those who use
   automation for skill development or to balance gameplay with real-life
   commitments, not encourage permanently automated characters.

   See &+Yhelp robots&n for guidance.

&+C6. PvP and racewars&n

   Player killing and corpse looting are expected parts of Duris. Resolve
   ordinary in-game rivalries through play, within these rules. PvP does
   not excuse harassment, real-world threats, or other misconduct.

   Wait at least &+Yone hour&n after logging off before logging on a character
   on the opposite side of the racewar.

   Do not use an opposite-side character to spy for your primary side or
   to take revenge on its behalf.

   After a PvP death, wait at least &+Yone real-life hour&n before logging in
   another character to take revenge or assist retaliation. This applies
   even when both characters are on the same racewar side, including
   returning to an area where the same PvP encounter is reasonably
   expected. See &+Yhelp multi-playing&n for further guidance.

   &+YCross-racewar intelligence sharing is prohibited.&n Players must not
   knowingly provide information to the opposing side that gives them an
   unfair tactical advantage. This includes revealing planned attacks,
   disclosing player or group movements, warning enemies of impending PvP
   or raids, or otherwise assisting the opposing side using information
   obtained through their own side.

   This applies to in-game communication as well as external platforms
   such as Discord, private messages and voice chat. Friendships across
   racewar sides are perfectly acceptable, but players are expected to
   respect the competitive integrity of the racewar.

&+C7. Equipment and artifacts&n

   Transferring equipment or artifacts between the good and evil racewar
   sides is prohibited, whether directly or through other characters or
   players.

   An exception may be considered in circumstances of significant racewar
   imbalance. Duris recognises and appreciates players who voluntarily
   switch sides to help maintain a healthy and competitive racewar.

   Where such an exception is proposed, the immortal team will announce it
   on Discord and provide the playerbase with a reasonable opportunity to
   discuss the proposal before any decision is made. This discussion may
   include whether equipment and artifacts should accompany the character
   changing sides.

   Exceptions will generally only be approved where there is broad
   community support and the transfer is considered beneficial to overall
   racewar balance. They are not intended to provide individual players
   with an equipment advantage or an opportunity to circumvent normal game
   rules.

   Ultimately, the immortal team retains final discretion over whether an
   exception is granted, including what equipment or artifacts, if any,
   may be transferred. Decisions will be made with fairness, transparency
   and player consultation in mind.

   Players are not otherwise required to move artifacts between their
   characters when switching characters. See &+Yhelp artifact&n for the general
   artifact policy.

&+C8. Punishment evasion&n

   Players must not attempt to evade bans, silences or other disciplinary
   restrictions imposed by immortals.

   This includes using alternative characters, accounts, connections or
   other players to circumvent an active punishment.

   VPN use is permitted, provided it is not used to evade disciplinary
   restrictions.

&+C9. Immortals and active players&n

   &+YServing as an immortal and actively playing are mutually exclusive.&n

   Players who hold an immortal character or immortal-level privileges may
   not actively play mortal characters. Anyone actively playing a mortal
   character may not simultaneously serve as an immortal.

   This restriction does not extend to developers, coders, zone builders
   or other contributors who do not hold immortal characters or
   privileges. We encourage players to contribute to the development and
   improvement of Duris without having to give up playing the game.

   All contributors are expected to act fairly and must not abuse
   privileged access or non-public information to gain an unfair in-game
   advantage.

   These restrictions exist to prevent conflicts of interest, protect
   competitive integrity and maintain the playerbase's trust in fair
   administration.

&+C10. Reporting and enforcement&n
   Use &+Ypetition&n to report misconduct or ask Staff for clarification.
   Provide an honest account and any relevant logs; do not fabricate
   evidence or knowingly make false reports.
   Staff generally do not intervene in ordinary gameplay disputes, but
   they may act on misconduct even when no rule names the exact situation.
   Respect Staff decisions and raise concerns calmly through petition.
   Penalties depend on the circumstances and may include warnings,
   silencing, loss of equipment, frags or levels, deletion, or a ban.

&+c======================================================================&n
&+CSee also:&n &+YMULTI-PLAYING, ROBOTS, RACEWARS, RAID, ARTIFACT, PETITION&n
